C++ syntax with implementation notes:

```c++
struct LargeObject {
  int large_array[10000];
  LargeObject() { /* Constructor */ }
  LargeObject(const LargeObject&) { /* Copy Constructor */ }
  ~LargeObject() { /* Destructor */ }
};

LargeObject createLargeObject() {
  LargeObject obj; 
  // ... initialize obj ...
  return obj; // NRVO likely to occur here
}

LargeObject createLargeObject2() { return LargeObject{}; } // RVO likely to occur here
```
Note: The compiler might or might not perform RVO/NRVO, depending on optimization flags and implementation.  Explicitly requesting a copy (using std::move) would prevent the optimization.
